# Long-term experiment record -- what is versioned and what is deliberately NOT.
#
# The workspace is 82 GB, almost all of it corpora and weights.  Git is used here for the RECORD
# (facts, conclusions, scripts, notebooks, small result files, manifests), never for the data.  Data is
# made ADDRESSABLE instead of versioned: state/CORPUS_MANIFEST.json and state/CORPUS64_MANIFEST.json
# name exactly which dataset/kernel produced which rows, and `scripts/corpus*_manifest.py --check`
# re-verifies it against the platform.

# ---------------- corpora and weights: never versioned ----------------
corpus/
corpus64/
*.pt
*.pth
*.safetensors
*.zip
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.bin

# ---------------- SECRETS: must never leave this machine ----------------
# state/autodl_token.txt is an AutoDL *billing* credential (it was measured to be able to read the
# wallet balance and, for Pro instances, power them off).  A private repo is still a leak surface, so
# it is excluded by filename rather than trusted to stay private.
state/autodl_token.txt
state/autodl.json
**/access_token
**/kaggle.json
**/autodl_ed25519*
*.pem
*.key

# ---------------- competition data: not ours to redistribute ----------------
# data/raw/ holds the official train.csv / train_series.csv.  Competition rules restrict passing the
# Data around, and a private repo is still a copy on a third-party service.  It has no archival value
# either -- it re-downloads from the competition page in seconds -- so the cheap and prudent choice is
# to leave it out.
data/raw/

# ---------------- transient / noisy ----------------
.testtmp/
*.log
*_urls.tsv
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.egg-info/
.venv/
.pytest_cache/

# ---------------- caches and scratch areas (measured, not guessed) ----------------
# A first `git add -A` staged 6.5 GB, almost all of it HuggingFace model blobs duplicated ~15 times
# (84 MB each) inside per-run caches.  Those are reproducible downloads, not records.
.hf/
**/.hf/
**/hub/
# outputs/_landing alone was 9.2 GB across 4451 files -- a landing/scratch tree, not results.
outputs/_landing/
**/.cache/

# Vendored Python environments that came down with other people's artifacts (opencv's .so bundles
# etc., 63 MB each and duplicated per run).  Dependencies, not results.
**/_coat_env/
**/site-packages/
**/*.so
**/*.so.*
**/*.dll
**/*.dylib
**/*.libs/

# NOTE what is deliberately KEPT: *.md, *.py, *.ps1, *.ipynb, *.json, *.csv, and small *.npz.
# The .npz files are the raw OOF predictions -- 300 KB each and the actual evidence for every
# conclusion in FACTS.md.  The 300+ MB *.pt checkpoints next to them are excluded above: they are
# reproducible from the config recorded in the ledger, and the numbers are what matter.

# scratch commit-message files
state/cm.txt
state/commitmsg.txt
# ================= 2026-09-26 cleanup: payload vs record =================
# At 1526 tracked files the repo was 212 MB and 182 MB of that was `downloads/`.  The principle was
# already stated at the top of this file ("data is made ADDRESSABLE instead of versioned") -- but
# `downloads/` had never been added to it.
#
# !! NOTE FOR THE NEXT EDITOR: git does NOT support a trailing "#" comment on a pattern line.  The
# !! first attempt at this block put the reasons on the same line as the patterns, and every rule
# !! silently became an unmatchable pattern -- nothing was ignored and nothing changed.  Reasons go
# !! on their own comment lines only.
#
# KEPT under downloads/: *.npz (the raw OOF predictions, the evidence behind every FACTS entry),
# *.json (manifests and audits), *.py, *.md.

# raw arrays: intermediate, large, regenerable
downloads/**/*.npy
# label tables, re-downloadable from their datasets
downloads/**/*.parquet
# logs and dumps, not records
downloads/**/*.txt
# 83 MB of extensionless training blobs inside a pulled run
downloads/**/data/
downloads/**/*.pt
# rented-box scratch
downloads/rent/
# 6.7 MB, and the probe rebuilds it in 128 seconds
downloads/research/siteprobe/site_probe.csv
# raw API dumps, reproducible
downloads/research/*_raw*.json
# competition data: not ours to redistribute
downloads/**/train.csv
downloads/**/test.csv
downloads/**/sample_submission.csv
# scratch and old submissions
outputs/
# vendored dependencies, not results
_d4_env/
_coat_env/
# generated from ens_experiment.py plus a base notebook; the .json configs are the record
# NOTE the leading `**/`: the 2026-09-26 reorganisation moved this directory under kernels/, and a
# rule anchored at `kernel-exp/` silently stopped matching -- the symptom was twenty-four generated
# notebooks reappearing as untracked.  Moving content can invalidate ignore rules, so this is
# anchored loosely on purpose.
**/kernel-exp/**/*.ipynb
# local one-off pull directories, gathered here on 2026-09-26
scratch/

# ============ 2026-10-04: third-party downloads from the "who is above us" survey ============
# !! CAUGHT BY A DRY RUN, not by luck.  `git add -A` would have staged 64 files under work/above/:
# other people's NOTEBOOKS (bend-the-knee-to-dinov3-ensembled.ipynb, rsna-versia-5.ipynb,
# rsna-baseline-v15.ipynb, ...), other people's PIPELINE CODE (pipeline/blend.py,
# pipeline/public_raptor.py, reproduce/build.py, ...), their READMEs/manifests/recipe.json, and a
# 54 MB opencv wheel.  The rule already stated elsewhere in this project applies: their *findings*
# are recorded in our own words in docs/FIND-2026-10-04-what-is-above-us.md, but their ARTIFACTS
# are not ours to republish.
#
# Note WHY the existing rules did not catch these: *.zip/*.pt/*.bin are ignored, but *.ipynb,
# *.py and *.json are exactly the extensions this repo deliberately KEEPS.  A rule that excludes
# payload does not exclude third-party SOURCE.
#
# Nothing here has archival value -- every tree is re-downloadable in one command
# (`kaggle kernels pull <ref>` / `kaggle datasets download <ref>`) and the refs are recorded.
work/above/
work/cnx/
work/meniscus/
work/pub_new/

# Bulk scrapes of third-party usernames (356 teams above us and their members).  Public data, but
# bulk re-publication of other people's identities is the same call this repo already made about
# the leaderboard email addresses.  The aggregate numbers live in the FIND doc; the scripts that
# regenerate these files are kept.
work/above_us.json
work/above_us_public.json
work/top_teams_public.json

# Vendored dependency tree inside our own M448 run capture (398 MB). The numbers are in
# docs/PREREG-2026-10-03-m448-arm.md; the receipts stay.
work/cf448-out/**/_coat_env/


# scratch previews written by the kernel builders' --check mode
work/_*_preview.py

# raw Kaggle kernel log downloads (rendered copies live in work/klog_ab/*.txt)
work/klog_flat/
work/klog_ab/*/

# downloaded Kaggle Models for evaluation (keep the scripts, not the blobs)
work/models_axis/

# pulled third-party notebooks
work/newpub_1006/

# the public reader's 369 MB of checkpoints + wheels (re-fetchable via work/fetch_reader.py)
work/reader/
work/klog_rdr/
work/klog_f1/
work/klog_rdr2/
work/coat_probe/
work/models_axis/
work/distilled_dataset/
work/_gate_distilled_preview.py
work/newpub_1006/
work/lixin_ckpt/
work/stackpp_src/
work/stackpp_dataset/
work/_rdrtta_cell.py
work/klog_rdrtta/
